    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d211">

                <pb facs="0360" n="272" sameAs="frus:frus1892/pg272"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Wharton to Sir Julian Pauncefote.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1892-03-17"><hi rendition="#italic">March 17,
                        1892</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to refer to the discussion
                    which took place in the conferences lately held at this Department between the
                    Secretary of State, yourself, and the Canadian commissioners, respecting the
                    discriminating tolls in the Canadian canals 5 and to inclose herewith a <pb
                        facs="0361" n="273" xml:id="pg273"/> copy of a letter from the Lake
                    Carriers’ Association, dated Buffalo, N. Y., the 11th instant, containing
                    figures showing the amounts of the discrimination in question.</p>
                <p>The Department will greatly appreciate your courtesy in forwarding a copy of this
                    letter at once to the Canadian authorities for their information in connection
                    with the promised satisfactory adjustment of the question of canal tolls.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">William F.
                    Wharton.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d211-a1.xml" xpointer="d211-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
